 compare snapshot.shares_outstanding / data[-1].sharesIssued: if the ratio is an integer near 2/3/4/5/10 (±2%) and data[-1].split_adjustment_factor = 1.0, treat the row as in-flight and rely on snapshot.shares_outstanding for market-cap. We monitor this invariant daily with an internal alert. Please report any persistent mismatch (>5 business days) to feedback@edinetdb.jp. See docs/field-notes/latest_shares_snapshot.md.","quarter":1,"shares_outstanding":34459424,"shares_outstanding_excluding_treasury":33980084,"source":"latest_quarterly_earnings_disclosure","treasury_shares":479340},"non_consolidated_fields":["avg_annual_salary","dividend_per_share","payout_ratio_reported","shares_issued"],"period":"annual"}}